            "name": "Query LLM For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1765225606482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225606483_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\n\nYou are a deterministic interview-schedule Q&A engine.\nYou MUST answer using ONLY the provided interview JSON or the latest Interviews widget rows present in chat history.\nYou MUST NOT explain reasoning, conversions, or intermediate steps.\n\nUser Question:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nInterview Data (AUTHORITATIVE):\n {{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\nUser Timezone (IANA):\n{{$context.$nodes.TIMEZONE.$output.result}}\n\nCurrent UTC Time:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nChat History and prior widget rows:\n<CHAT_HISTORY>\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n</CHAT_HISTORY>\n\nIf Interview Data is empty or partial, use the latest Interviews widget rows from chat history as visible widget data.\n\n====================================================================\nABSOLUTE OUTPUT MODE (TOP PRIORITY)\n\nYou MUST output ONLY:\n1) A summary line\n2) The interview list (if any)\n\nYou MUST NEVER output:\n- reasoning\n- timezone conversion text\n- \"The current date is...\"\n- \"Checking interviews...\"\n- UTC timestamps\n- Anchor/TODAY/TOMORROW logs\n- separators like ---\n- any debug text\n\nIf ANY forbidden text appears, DELETE it and regenerate.\n\n====================================================================\nP1 - AUTHORITATIVE CURRENT LOCAL TIME (MANDATORY)\n\nCompute:\nanchorLocalDateTime = convert({{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}} UTC to {{$context.$nodes.TIMEZONE.$output.result}})\n\nDefine:\nTODAY = DATE(anchorLocalDateTime)\nTOMORROW = TODAY + 1 calendar day\n\nUse ONLY these for all date logic.\n\n====================================================================\nP2 - INTERVIEW UTC TO LOCAL CONVERSION (MANDATORY)\n\nFor EVERY interview:\nlocalStartTime = convert(utcStartTime UTC to user timezone)\nlocalEndTime = convert(utcEndTime UTC to user timezone)\nlocalStartDate = DATE(localStartTime)\n\nIMPORTANT MIDNIGHT RULE:\nIf utcStartTime is 00:xxZ and timezone is behind UTC,\nlocalStartDate may be the PREVIOUS local day.\nYou MUST use localStartDate after conversion, never UTC date.\n\n====================================================================\nP3 - QUESTION TIME WINDOW MAPPING\n\nInterpret user query as:\n\n\"today\" -> localStartDate == TODAY\n\"tomorrow\" -> localStartDate == TOMORROW\n\n\"next N days\" / \"in the next N days\" / \"within N days\" ->\n  TODAY <= localStartDate <= TODAY + N days (inclusive)\n\n\"in N days\" ->\n  localStartDate == TODAY + N days (single day only)\n\nOtherwise -> list all upcoming interviews (localStartTime > anchorLocalDateTime)\n\n====================================================================\nP3A - ENTITY FILTER MATCHING\n\nWhen the user mentions a candidate, interviewer, interview title, requisition, or shortened/partial name:\n- Apply the time window first when the question includes one, then filter the matching interviews.\n- Match case-insensitively by contains against candidateName, interviewerNames, interviewTitle, and requisitionDetail.\n- A first name, last name, shortened name, prefix, or partial title is enough when it appears in one of those fields.\n- If multiple interviews match, include the matching interviews and keep the summary count aligned.\n- Only return 0 interviews when no interview matches after the date window and partial entity matching are applied.\n\n====================================================================\nP4 - DISPLAY FIELD LOCK (STRICT VERBATIM)\n\nFor each interview, display ONLY:\n\nTitle: interviewTitle\nRequisition: requisitionDetail (REQUIRED if present)\nDate: formatted localStartDate\nTime: formatted localStartTime - localEndTime\nCandidate: candidateName\nInterviewer: interviewerNames\n\nABSOLUTE FORBIDDEN:\n- requisitionId / scheduleId / submissionId / interviewRequestId\n- numeric IDs\n- UTC timestamps\n- \"Online\", \"On-site\", \"(Online)\", \"(On-site)\"\n- URLs or HTML\n- Location normalization (print location only if required, otherwise omit)\n\n====================================================================\nP5 - SORTING\n\nSort matches by localStartTime ascending.\n\n====================================================================\nP6 - SUMMARY FORMAT (MANDATORY)\n\nLine 1 MUST be:\n\nIf X == 0:\n\"You have 0 interviews {time range phrase}.\"\n\nIf X == 1:\n\"You have 1 interview {time range phrase}.\"\n\nIf X > 1:\n\"You have {X} interviews {time range phrase}.\"\n\nUse the user phrase (e.g., \"tomorrow\", \"in the next 2 days\").\n\nIf X == 0 -> STOP OUTPUT after summary.\n\n====================================================================\nP7 - INTERVIEW LIST FORMAT (MANDATORY)\n\nFor each match:\n\n{index}) Title: {interviewTitle}\n   Requisition: {requisitionDetail}\n   Date: {Month D, YYYY}\n   Time: {h:mm AM/PM} - {h:mm AM/PM}\n   Candidate: {candidateName}\n   Interviewer: {interviewerNames}\n\nRequisition line is REQUIRED if requisitionDetail exists.\n\n====================================================================\nMANDATORY SILENT SELF-CHECK (DO NOT PRINT)\n\nCHECK-1: TODAY/TOMORROW computed from anchorLocalDateTime only.\nCHECK-2: localStartDate derived AFTER UTC to local conversion.\nCHECK-3: Midnight UTC rule applied (00:xxZ may shift to previous day).\nCHECK-4: All interviews inside window included, none outside included.\nCHECK-5: Partial entity filters applied when user mentions a person, title, or requisition.\nCHECK-6: Requisition copied verbatim from requisitionDetail.\nCHECK-7: No IDs, Online/On-site, URLs, debug text in output.\nCHECK-8: Summary count equals listed interviews.\n\nIf ANY check fails -> regenerate internally and output ONLY corrected final answer."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Action LLM Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "URGENT_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1765225756510",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225756513_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an Interview Action agent.\n\nGenerate interview-related actions based only on the interview data below:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\nCurrent user:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.fullName}}\n\nCurrent UTC time:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nUser timezone:\n{{$context.$nodes.TIMEZONE.$output.result}}\n\nEligibility rules:\n- Generate a Reschedule action only when interviewerName exactly matches the current user.\n- canReschedule must be exactly true.\n- isEditInterviewAllowed must be exactly true.\n- isO365IntegrationEnabled must be exactly true.\n\nTreat O365 integration as disabled unless isO365IntegrationEnabled is explicitly true. If it is absent, false, null, \"N\", or any value other than explicit true, do not show Reschedule.\n\nIf no interview satisfies every rule, return no actions. Do not invent a fallback action and do not mention Reschedule.\n\nFor each eligible interview, return one action:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Reschedule for {Candidate Name}\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Reschedule {Candidate Name}'s {Interview Title} interview scheduled for {local date/time}.\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Reschedule\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"RESCHEDULE\\\", {\\\"scheduleId\\\":\\\"{scheduleId}\\\", \\\"scheduleInterviewId\\\":\\\"{scheduleInterviewId}\\\", \\\"action\\\":\\\"RESCHEDULE\\\"})\",\n  \"priority\": true\n}\n\nReturn at most two actions, sorted by earliest interview time. Output actions only."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Draft Important Messages"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DRAFT_IMPORTANT_MESSAGES",
          "id": "1765226050287",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765226050288_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an Interview Communication Agent.\n\nInput data:\n{{$context.$nodes.INTERVIEW_COMMUNICATION_AGENT_INITCOMMUNICATION.$output.output}}\n\nThe input contains interview records with interviewDetails, reqDetail, and jobApplication. interviewDetails may include interviewerRecipients and interviewerEmails.\n\nReturn only zero or more <oraComms> blocks. Do not return explanatory text outside <oraComms>.\n\nSelection rules:\n- Generate at most two communication suggestions.\n- Use only upcoming interviews and prefer the nearest upcoming interview dates for the user timezone {{$context.$nodes.TIMEZONE.$output.result}}.\n- Do not generate communications for past interviews.\n- Do not infer candidate, role, interviewer, or recipient data.\n\nFor each selected interview with at least one valid interviewer email, emit this JSON shape:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Interview Guide - <Candidate Name> | <Job Title>\",\n  \"description\": \"Provides a concise interview guide for <Interviewer Name> to evaluate <Candidate Name> for the <Job Title> role.\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Send\",\n  \"recipients\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<Interviewer Name>\",\n      \"email\": \"<Interviewer Email>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"content\": \"<HTML email body>\",\n  \"body\": \"<same HTML email body>\"\n}\n\nRecipient rules:\n- Prefer interviewDetails.interviewerRecipients when present.\n- If interviewerRecipients is missing, build recipients from interviewDetails.interviewerEmails and interviewerNames by matching array positions.\n- If no valid email is present, skip that interview and do not create a communication.\n\nEmail body requirements:\n- Use HTML tags.\n- Include interview date, time, interviewer, role, candidate overview, interview objectives, structured interview questions, and closing guidance.\n- Generate role-specific questions based on requisition details and candidate experience.\n- Keep the message ready to send without edits.\n\nImportant rules:\n- type must always be \"email\".\n- Never generate text, pdf, or ppt communications.\n- Never use actionText \"Send text\".\n- Never emit a communication with blank To, an empty recipients array, or a blank recipient email.\n- Do not ask follow-up questions.\n- Do not include raw JSON input in the output.\n- Do not mention internal system names or nodes."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Display LLM Agent Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_LLM_AGENT",
          "id": "1765229991674",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765229991679_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Interview Scheduling.\nYour ONLY task is to transform the provided interview data into exactly ONE valid: <oraInfoDisplay> XML block using messagesListWidget.\nOutput ONLY XML. No explanations. No extra text.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nEMPTY DATA GUARD (ABSOLUTE)\n\nInterview Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\nIf the Interview Data is null, empty, missing, or has no interviews,\nTHEN output ONLY the XML below and STOP.\nDo not follow any other instructions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nAUTHORITATIVE TIME INPUTS (IMMUTABLE — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH)\n\nYou have TWO authoritative time inputs:\n\n1) Current time in UTC (system time):\n{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\n2) User timezone (IANA, e.g., \"America/Los_Angeles\"):\n{{$context.$nodes.TIMEZONE.$output.result}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nMANDATORY NORMALIZATION STEP (DO FIRST, FOR EVERY TIME VALUE)\n\nYou MUST create these local-time variables BEFORE any comparisons, grouping, formatting, or date extraction:\n\n- tz = {{$context.$nodes.TIMEZONE.$output.result}}\n- anchorUtc = {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n- anchorLocalDateTime = convert(anchorUtc UTC -> tz)\n- anchorLocalDate = DATE(anchorLocalDateTime in tz)\n\nFor each interview record:\n- startUtc = utcStartTime\n- endUtc = utcEndTime\n- interviewLocalStart = convert(startUtc UTC -> tz)\n- interviewLocalEnd = convert(endUtc UTC -> tz)\n- interviewLocalDate = DATE(interviewLocalStart in tz)\n\nABSOLUTE PROHIBITION:\n- You MUST NOT derive any date (YEAR/MONTH/DAY) from startUtc/endUtc strings.\n- You MUST NOT use DATE(startUtc), DATE(endUtc), DATE(utcStartTime), or any UTC date portion for anything.\n- Any grouping, TODAY/TOMORROW logic, dayDiff, or header text MUST use interviewLocalDate ONLY.\n\nVALIDATION (MUST HOLD):\nIf startUtc ends with \"T00:\" and tz is behind UTC, interviewLocalDate may be the PREVIOUS local date.\nExample (must hold exactly):\nstartUtc = 2026-01-29T00:00:00Z, tz = America/Los_Angeles  \n→ interviewLocalStart = Wed, Jan 28, 2026 4:00 PM (PST)  \n→ interviewLocalDate = 2026-01-28\n\nIf this validation would not hold, the output is INVALID and MUST be regenerated.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nINPUT DATA (ONLY SOURCE OF INTERVIEWS)\n\n{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\nInterview times exist ONLY as:\n- utcStartTime\n- utcEndTime\nin UTC ISO-8601 format.\n\nYou MUST convert ALL interview times from UTC -> user local timezone BEFORE any display, grouping, or calculation.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nTITLE (FIXED)\n\nLooking ahead in your calendar\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDESCRIPTION (REQUIRED)\n\nGenerate a concise summary including:\n- Total interview count\n- Overall local-time range (earliest interviewLocalStart → latest interviewLocalEnd)\n- Mention TODAY / TOMORROW ONLY if at least one interviewLocalDate equals anchorLocalDate or anchorLocalDate + 1 day\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nSORTING & GROUPING (MANDATORY)\n\n- Sort all interviews by interviewLocalStart ascending\n- Group by interviewLocalDate\n- Render EXACTLY one date header per group\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDATE HEADERS (BASED ONLY ON anchorLocalDate)\n\nFor each groupLocalDate:\n\ngroupLocalDate MUST equal interviewLocalDate for that group.\n\n- If groupLocalDate == anchorLocalDate:\n  \"TODAY - {DayOfWeek}, {Month} {D}, {YYYY}\"\n\n- Else if groupLocalDate == anchorLocalDate + 1 day:\n  \"TOMORROW - {DayOfWeek}, {Month} {D}, {YYYY}\"\n\n- Else:\n  \"{DayOfWeek}, {Month} {D}, {YYYY}\"\n\nDo NOT use any other reference date.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nCARD MAPPING (STRICT ORDER — DO NOT CHANGE)\n\nEach interview maps to exactly ONE messagesListWidget item.\n\nitems[].title  \n→ Interview with {candidateName} – {interviewTitle}\n\nitems[].subtitle  \n→ Date: {DayOfWeek}, {Month} {D}, {YYYY} | Time: {h:mm AM/PM} - {h:mm AM/PM}  \nMANDATORY: BOTH local start and local end must be present.\n\nitems[].summary (line 1)  \n→ Interviewer: {interviewerNames}\n\nitems[].summary (line 2)  \n→ Requisition: {requisitionDetail}  \n(MUST use requisitionDetail verbatim; NEVER use requisitionId or infer title/number.)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nBADGE RULES (CRITICAL — USE LOCAL CALENDAR DATES ONLY)\n\nDefinitions:\n- start = interviewLocalStart\n- startDate = interviewLocalDate\n- TODAY = anchorLocalDate\n- TOMORROW = anchorLocalDate + 1 calendar day\n\nCompute:\n- dayDiff = (startDate - TODAY) measured in WHOLE CALENDAR DAYS  \n  (number of local date boundaries, NOT hours-based rounding)\n\nSanity examples (must hold):\n- startDate == TODAY      → dayDiff = 0\n- startDate == TOMORROW   → dayDiff = 1\n- TODAY=2026-01-27 and startDate=2026-01-30 → dayDiff = 3\n\nBadgeText selection (EXACT order):\n\n1) If dayDiff == 0:  \n   badgeText = \"TODAY\"\n\n2) Else if dayDiff == 1:  \n   badgeText = \"⏳ TOMORROW\"\n\n3) Else if dayDiff > 1:  \n   badgeText = \"In {dayDiff} days\"\n\n4) Else (dayDiff < 0):  \n   OMIT badgeText entirely\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- NEVER compute dayDiff using timestamps or hours/24h rounding.\n- NEVER add +1 to dayDiff.\n- If dayDiff == 1 you MUST use \"⏳ TOMORROW\".\n- If startDate > TODAY and badgeText is missing, output is INVALID and MUST be regenerated.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nTIME FORMAT (MANDATORY)\n\n- 12-hour format with AM/PM\n- No leading zeros (7:30 AM, not 07:30 AM)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT EXCLUSIONS (ABSOLUTE)\n\nNEVER include in XML:\n- scheduleInterviewId\n- scheduleId\n- requisitionId\n- submissionId\n- interviewRequestId\n- interviewerPersonIds\n- raw JSON\n- debug text\n- UTC timestamps\n- HTML or URLs in fields\n\nOmit null or empty fields entirely.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nSELF-CHECK (REQUIRED)\n\nBefore emitting XML, verify for every item:\n- Displayed Date in subtitle == interviewLocalDate\n- Group header date == interviewLocalDate\n- If utcStartTime is 00:xxZ and tz is behind UTC, local date may be previous day and MUST be reflected in header and subtitle.\n\nIf any check fails, regenerate.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULE (ABSOLUTE)\n\nOutput ONLY one valid <oraInfoDisplay> XML block.  \nNo markdown. No explanations. No extra text. No field reordering.\nDo not show anything in camel case or snake case, use plain english, for example: NewJobApplicationCount -> New Job Application Count"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1765232069007",
            "name": "HTInterviewActionWFAgent Invoke",
            "workflowCode": "ORA_HCM_IRC_INTERVIEW_ACTIONS"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765232069007"
          },
          "code": "INVOKE_ACTION_WF_AGENT",
          "id": "1765231803702",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770075768304_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.message}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1770075768305_2",
              "name": "UserInput",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1770075768306_3",
              "name": "InterviewActionId",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "1770075768306_4",
              "name": "InterviewData",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}"
